# Python style

- Imports: stdlib, third party, local (`I` via ruff). Absolute imports from `vocab.*`.
- Naming: `snake_case` functions/vars, `PascalCase` classes, `UPPER_SNAKE` constants.
- Docstrings: one-line or short paragraph explaining **why**, not a restatement of the signature.
- Prefer early returns over deep nesting.
- No bare `except:`. Log then fail closed for user-facing paths.
- Pydantic models for request bodies and structured LLM output; validate at the boundary.
- FastAPI: declare dependencies explicitly; keep handlers under ~40 lines when practical by calling services.
